# ECAPA-TDNN Evaluation & Changes Report

This document contains both the speaker verification evaluation results for the pre-trained ECAPA-TDNN model on the **VoxCeleb** dataset, and a breakdown of the codebase changes required to run it successfully.

---

## 1. Final Evaluation Results

> [!TIP]
> The **EER Threshold** represents the optimal cosine similarity score to decide whether two voices belong to the same speaker. A score above `0.311` means "match", and below means "no match".

| Metric | Value | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **EER Threshold** | `0.311101` | The ideal cosine similarity decision threshold |
| **EER (Equal Error Rate)** | `0.97%` | The rate where False Acceptances equal False Rejections |
| **minDCF** | `0.0717%` | Minimum Detection Cost Function (a standard metric for NIST evaluations) |


### Error Curve Analysis (FAR vs FRR)

The intersection between the False Acceptance Rate (FAR, blue) and the False Rejection Rate (FRR, red) represents the Equal Error Rate point. The vertical green line indicates our optimal decision threshold.

